// pfodWeb NOTE: excludes GPIO14-19/28-31/34/35/45/49-52/54 - dedicated
// onboard Ethernet PHY and ESP32-C6 WiFi companion SDIO/SDMMC pins
// (see vendor pins_arduino.h ETH_*/BOARD_SDIO_*/BOARD_SDMMC_* lines).
// INDEPENDENTLY CONFIRMED (2026-07-14): GPIO14/15/16/17/18/19/54 match
// Espressif's own esp-hosted-mcu docs (github.com/espressif/esp-hosted-mcu,
// docs/esp32_p4_function_ev_board.md - "GPIOs: CLK[18] CMD[19] D0[14]
// D1[15] D2[16] D3[17] Slave_Reset[54]" for the SDIO link to the onboard
// ESP32-C6-MINI-1 WiFi/BT companion). GPIO28/29/30/31/34/35/49/50/51/52
// match techoverflow.net's "ESP32-P4: Which GPIOs to use for RMII" writeup
// (CRS_DV=28, RXD0=29, RXD1=30, MDC=31, TXD0=34, TXD1=35, TX_EN=49,
// REF_CLK=50, PHY reset=51 (IP101GRI), MDIO=52) for this board's IP101
// Ethernet PHY. GPIO45 (SDMMC power) matches the official Espressif
// ESP32-P4-Function-EV-Board Owner's Manual (via device.report), which
// documents GPIO45 as the SD_PWRn microSD-slot power-control line
// (only freed for GPIO use by moving resistor R231->R100 on the board).
